The database is still queried twice per request. Why?

The user sees "Could not save" even though the row is created successfully. Why?

```jsx
'use server'
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation'

export async function save(prev, formData) {
  try {
    const post = await db.post.create({ data: parse(formData) })
    redirect('/posts/' + post.id)
  } catch (err) {
    return { error: 'Could not save' }
  }
}
```

